ng in this country it's it's  difficult to see what's happened  over the last six months and not feel  some sort of call to action  so for me the the reason that's this  most important election ever is because  there are so many people like me who  look like me who cannot have their  voices heard  so i want to be able to to  to make sure that what i'm impressing on  the people that i speak to  is that important um you know  there are so many different issues that  are circling the united states right now  whether it's immigration  the economy covid um the health care  the trade war um all of these things  that happened  over the last ten years the last three  and a half years that we have to deal  with  um and you know the we're at a unique  place in history where technology  um society have all just converged in  different ways and we have  a lot of work to do and that's why 2020  is the most important election ever to  me  but absolutely ever yes that was great  yes yes and that's a great place to wrap  it up  um i just want to thank maddie mills for  joining me today to preview tonight's  election results  thank you to all of our guests for  taking the time to talk to us  and thank you the viewers for tuning in  with us these last seven weeks  i'll remind you once more if you haven't  please please please go vote it takes  just a few minutes to make your voice  heard  in the most important election ever i'm  ever white  for bloomberg quick take thanks for  joining us guys


